# 描述: 必考词Unit29核心词汇

{{renew}}{{/rɪˈnjuː}}{{v. 更新； renew；续签}}{{I need to renew my subscription.}}
{{renovate}}{{/ˈrenəveɪt}}{{v. 翻新； renovate；修复}}{{The old building was renovated.}}
{{reputation}}{{/ˌrepjuˈteɪʃn}}{{n. 名声； reputation；声誉}}{{The company has an excellent reputation.}}
{{request}}{{/rɪˈkwest}}{{n./v. 请求； request}}{{She submitted a request for leave.}}
{{require}}{{/rɪˈkwaɪər}}{{v. 需要； require；要求}}{{The job requires experience.}}
{{rescue}}{{/ˈreskjuː}}{{v./n. 营救； rescue}}{{The team rescued the trapped miners.}}
{{resemble}}{{/rɪˈzembl}}{{v. 像； resemble；类似于}}{{She resembles her mother.}}
{{resent}}{{/rɪˈzent}}{{v. 怨恨； resent；不满}}{{He resented the unfair treatment.}}
{{reserve}}{{/rɪˈzɜːv}}{{v./n. 保留； reserve；储备}}{{I'd like to reserve a table.}}
{{reside}}{{/rɪˈzaɪd}}{{v. 居住； reside；存在于}}{{The family resides in London.}}
{{resign}}{{/rɪˈzaɪn}}{{v. 辞职； resign；顺从}}{{He resigned from his position.}}
{{resist}}{{/rɪˈzɪst}}{{v. 抵抗； resist；抵制}}{{The army resisted the attack.}}
{{resolve}}{{/rɪˈzɒlv}}{{v./n. 决心； resolve；解决}}{{They resolved the conflict peacefully.}}
{{resource}}{{/rɪˈsɔːs}}{{n. 资源； resource}}{{The country is rich in resources.}}
{{respond}}{{/rɪˈspɒnd}}{{v. 回应； respond；回答}}{{She responded to the email promptly.}}
{{restore}}{{/rɪˈstɔːr}}{{v. 恢复； restore；修复}}{{The temple was restored to its original condition.}}
{{restrain}}{{/rɪˈstreɪn}}{{v. 抑制； restrain；限制}}{{He restrained his anger.}}
{{restrict}}{{/rɪˈstrɪkt}}{{v. 限制； restrict；约束}}{{Access is restricted to authorized personnel.}}
{{retain}}{{/rɪˈteɪn}}{{v. 保留； retain；保持}}{{The company retained its best employees.}}
{{retreat}}{{/rɪˈtriːt}}{{v./n. 撤退； retreat； retreat}}{{The army was forced to retreat.}}
{{retrieve}}{{/rɪˈtriːv}}{{v. 检索； retrieve；取回}}{{You can retrieve the file from the server.}}
{{reveal}}{{/rɪˈviːl}}{{v. 揭示； reveal；透露}}{{The investigation revealed the truth.}}
{{revenue}}{{/ˈrevənjuː}}{{n. 收入； revenue；税收}}{{Revenue increased by 20% this year.}}
{{reverse}}{{/rɪˈvɜːs}}{{v./adj./n. 颠倒； reverse；相反的}}{{The court reversed the decision.}}
{{revise}}{{/rɪˈvaɪz}}{{v. 修订； revise；修改}}{{The report was revised to include new data.}}
{{revive}}{{/rɪˈvaɪv}}{{v. 复兴； revive；恢复}}{{The government tried to revive the economy.}}
{{revolution}}{{/ˌrevəˈluːʃn}}{{n. 革命； revolution；旋转}}{{The digital revolution changed everything.}}
{{rhetoric}}{{/ˈretərɪk}}{{n. 修辞； rhetoric；花言巧语}}{{His speech was full of rhetoric.}}
{{rigid}}{{/ˈrɪdʒɪd}}{{adj. 严格的； rigid；僵硬的}}{{The rules are too rigid.}}
{{rival}}{{/ˈraɪvl}}{{n./v. 竞争对手； rival；与…匹敌}}{{The two companies are fierce rivals.}}
{{robust}}{{/rəʊˈbʌst}}{{adj. 强健的； robust；坚固的}}{{The economy showed robust growth.}}
{{rotate}}{{/rəʊˈteɪt}}{{v. 旋转； rotate；轮换}}{{The earth rotates on its axis.}}
{{routine}}{{/ruːˈtiːn}}{{n./adj. 日常的； routine；惯例}}{{Exercise is part of my daily routine.}}
{{ruin}}{{/ˈruːɪn}}{{v./n. 毁灭； ruin；废墟}}{{The scandal ruined his reputation.}}
{{sacrifice}}{{/ˈsækrɪfaɪs}}{{v./n. 牺牲； sacrifice；献祭}}{{She sacrificed her free time for the project.}}
