{{staff}}{{/stɑːf}}{{n./v. 员工； staff；配备人员}}{{The hospital is fully staffed.}}
{{stake}}{{/steɪk}}{{n. 利害关系； stake；赌注}}{{He has a stake in the outcome.}}
{{stale}}{{/steɪl}}{{adj. 不新鲜的； stale；陈旧的}}{{The bread has gone stale.}}
{{stall}}{{/stɔːl}}{{v./n. 停滞； stall；摊位}}{{The negotiations stalled.}}
{{standard}}{{/ˈstændəd}}{{n./adj. 标准； standard；标准的}}{{The product meets high standards.}}
{{statistic}}{{/stəˈtɪstɪk}}{{n. 统计数据； statistic}}{{The statistics show a clear trend.}}
{{status}}{{/ˈsteɪtəs}}{{n. 地位； status；状态}}{{The project's status is under review.}}
{{steady}}{{/ˈstedi}}{{adj./v. 稳定的； steady；使稳定}}{{The economy has shown steady improvement.}}
{{stem}}{{/stem}}{{n./v. 茎； stem；源于}}{{Many problems stem from poor planning.}}
{{stern}}{{/stɜːn}}{{adj. 严厉的； stern；坚定的}}{{The teacher gave a stern warning.}}
{{stimulate}}{{/ˈstɪmjuleɪt}}{{v. 刺激； stimulate；激发}}{{The policy stimulates economic growth.}}
{{straightforward}}{{/ˌstreɪtˈfɔːwəd}}{{adj. 直接的； straightforward；简单的}}{{The process is straightforward.}}
{{strain}}{{/streɪn}}{{n./v. 压力； strain；拉紧}}{{The workload is a strain on staff.}}
{{strategy}}{{/ˈstrætədʒi}}{{n. 策略； strategy；战略}}{{The company adopted a new strategy.}}
{{strengthen}}{{/ˈstreŋθn}}{{v. 加强； strengthen}}{{Exercise strengthens the body.}}
{{stress}}{{/stres}}{{n./v. 压力； stress；强调}}{{She is under a lot of stress.}}
{{strict}}{{/strɪkt}}{{adj. 严格的； strict；严谨的}}{{The school has strict rules.}}
{{stride}}{{/straɪd}}{{n./v. 大步； stride；进步}}{{The company made great strides in research.}}
{{strike}}{{/straɪk}}{{v./n. 罢工； strike；打击}}{{The workers went on strike.}}
{{strive}}{{/straɪv}}{{v. 努力； strive；奋斗}}{{We must strive for excellence.}}
{{structure}}{{/ˈstrʌktʃər}}{{n./v. 结构； structure；组织}}{{The company restructured its operations.}}
